p8", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 57082, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01X3gpi1gu7JRpftkRjCPvp8", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 59234, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01DNFJVWpTz77rwQrPR2X9C4", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 59534, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01DNFJVWpTz77rwQrPR2X9C4", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 59534, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01DNFJVWpTz77rwQrPR2X9C4", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 64530, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0, its most recent healthy release, in all regions. SEV2 incident INC-0001 is open.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of about 18%. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) was also unhealthy, so v2.3.0 was the latest healthy version.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. That left us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1.\n- I tried the rollback once more, which is safe because it only moves to a known-healthy version. It finished in all three regions.\n- All three regions now run v2.3.0. The service reports healthy and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to open the incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so I didn't send it again and page on-call twice.\n- INC-0001 covers what went wrong, the partial rollback and the retry, and the current state. It also lists two follow-ups: find what broke v2.3.1, and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01KmgYJWCmnPK9jz9AXNqMMW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_015goXFRe6bwTq7tfJtoou3D", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01LGzQxmyV1peq8qdY3zqbzx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01V7Wxq2drG8ZjqZkNHr26D7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway through. us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to a known-healthy release is safe to repeat, so I'll try once more.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01SVxXcbWK7zQvm2DWnf7NbS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01NNh7wMUqbXeEfbxdX2Zy7H", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_017rqSoyJKfaYLFM7ByWt3Kv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01X3gpi1gu7JRpftkRjCPvp8", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, which left the regions on mixed versions (us-east v2.3.0, us-west/eu-west v2.3.1). A second attempt finished. All three regions now run v2.3.0, the service is healthy and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression, and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, so it may or may not have been created. I'll check before retrying so the on-call engineer isn't paged twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01DNFJVWpTz77rwQrPR2X9C4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0, its most recent healthy release, in all regions. SEV2 incident INC-0001 is open.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of about 18%. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) was also unhealthy, so v2.3.0 was the latest healthy version.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. That left us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1.\n- I tried the rollback once more, which is safe because it only moves to a known-healthy version. It finished in all three regions.\n- All three regions now run v2.3.0. The service reports healthy and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to open the incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so I didn't send it again and page on-call twice.\n- INC-0001 covers what went wrong, the partial rollback and the retry, and the current state. It also lists two follow-ups: find what broke v2.3.1, and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}